 medical guidance**\\n\\nI need to create a concise summary with medical caution. It's important to mention the suggestion to use the LLM distillation tool since it was run during the discussion of the symptoms. The symptoms are minimal, so I’ll keep that in mind. Following instructions, I should suggest the distillation tool and possibly include a media URL as MEDIA:url to support the summary. It's crucial to be clear and helpful!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done — I ran the kidney cancer detection pipeline on your image.\n\n**Kidney Cancer Detector**\n- **Kidney cancer class:** `kidney_tumor`\n- **Confidence:** **99.9979%**\n- **Inference time:** **3.27 s**\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Prediction:** `kidney_tumor`\n- **CAM coverage:** 0.0128\n- **CAM center ratio:** 0.8250\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** 0.1000\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 1.0000\n- **CAM explanation:** the model focused on a localized central renal region with asymmetric distribution, which it interpreted as a visually distinct area possibly consistent with a localized structural alteration.\n\n**X-AI module**\n- **Confidence interpretation:** the model reports very high confidence, but this is **not a definitive diagnosis**.\n- **Summary:** the pipeline output suggests a high likelihood of kidney cancer and identifies visual evidence of a kidney tumor.\n- **Recommended next steps:**\n  1. Further medical evaluation with imaging/lab review\n  2. Discuss the result with a medical professional\n  3. Consider additional tests such as biopsy or genetic testing if clinically appropriate\n\n**Important note**\nThis is a **preliminary prototype tool output, not an actual diagnosis**. A radiologist/urologist review and proper clinical workup are still needed to confirm what this image represents.\n\nIf you want, I can now help you **interpret this result in clinical context**, or you can run the **LLM Distillation** step to turn this pipeline output into a clearer patient-facing