 I can leverage that up-to-date understanding to help with the task at hand effectively! Let's see what I can come up with.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] If the image is **not uploaded successfully first**, the rest of this skill will usually **fail or become unreliable**, because the prototype request depends on the uploaded remote image path.\n\nIn practice, the chain is:\n\n1. **Upload step creates the remote file path**\n   - The skill sends the image to the upload endpoint.\n   - It then builds the image path from `path + filename`.\n\n2. **That path is inserted into the prototype request**\n   - The fixed JSON contains an image placeholder.\n   - If upload did not work, there is no valid image path to substitute.\n\n3. **Prototype execution then has no valid image to read**\n   - Best case: the endpoint returns an error or empty/failed downstream output.\n   - Worse case: if a stale or wrong path were used, the pipeline could analyze the wrong file.\n\nSo the upload step is effectively a **required dependency** for:\n- the **Kidney Cancer Detector**\n- the **Image Analyzer**\n- the **X-AI summary**\n\nWithout a valid uploaded image, those modules should not be trusted.\n\nIn this skill specifically, the intended safe behavior is:\n- upload image first\n- read the upload response\n- build the remote path\n- only then execute the prototype payload with that path\n\nIf you want, I can also explain the **exact failure modes** you might see at each step:\n- **upload endpoint failure**\n- **successful upload but malformed returned path**\n- **prototype runs but downstream nodes produce misleading output**","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0bfb0597f02b52410169bac0cdb1708191af712642a87f8d76\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":13533,"output":340,"cacheRead":9344,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23217,"cost":{"input":0.0338325,"output":0.0051,"cacheRead":0.002